WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.060
An eye for an eye.

2
00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:06.030
In ancient law, that rule
set a limit on revenge.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.790
Then Jesus says: But I tell you,
don't resist him who is evil.

4
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.480
Turn the other cheek.

5
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:17.510
And more: love your enemies, and
pray for those who persecute you.

6
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.610
Is that a command from
God that must be obeyed?

7
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.830
Or advice from a wise human teacher?

8
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.350
In this mission, you'll read his
teaching on revenge and enemies closely,

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.110
and ask what follows if his
authority is only human.

10
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.760
Then you'll see how Christians
apply turn the other cheek today,

11
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.860
in very different ways.

12
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.750
Your mission: work out where the
authority of love your enemies comes from,

13
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.200
for different Christians.
